meta {
  name: 02. Get Weather Forecast
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/groups/{{hamyarGroupId}}/hamyar/weather?lat=35.6892&lng=51.3890&start_date={{startDate}}&end_date={{endDate}}
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

vars:pre-request {
  endDate: 2026-11-22
  startDate: 2026-11-19
}

settings {
  encodeUrl: true
  timeout: 0
  forwardAuthorizationHeader: false
}

docs {
  ## Method, Endpoint, and Authentication
  
  `GET /api/v1/groups/{groupID}/hamyar/weather?lat=<latitude>&lng=<longitude>&start_date=<YYYY-MM-DD>&end_date=<YYYY-MM-DD>` — requires a Bearer access token; requester must own the group. `groupID` is the positive integer ID of the group whose owner is making the request.
  
  Returns current conditions and a daily forecast from Open-Meteo for the supplied WGS84 coordinates and requested date range. Both dates are required and must be today or a future date no later than 14 days from today (inclusive); `end_date` must be on or after `start_date`. Date-only values are checked against the UTC calendar date. Daily dates and current observation time use the timezone resolved for the coordinates. Temperatures are Celsius, wind speed is km/h, and precipitation is measured in millimeters.
  
  ## Query parameters
  
  | Parameter | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `lat` | `number` | Yes | WGS84 latitude from -90 through 90, inclusive. |
  | `lng` | `number` | Yes | WGS84 longitude from -180 through 180, inclusive. |
  | `start_date` | `string` | Yes | Forecast start date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format; today through 14 days from today, inclusive. |
  | `end_date` | `string` | Yes | Forecast end date in `YYYY-MM-DD` format; on or after `start_date` and no later than 14 days from today, inclusive. |
  
  ## Successful response
  
  **`200 OK`** — returns the resolved coordinates and timezone, current conditions, unit labels, and parallel daily forecast arrays. Each index in a daily array corresponds to the date at the same index in `daily.time`. `weather_code` values are WMO weather interpretation codes. The response may contain fewer dates if the provider has fewer forecast days available.
  
  | Field | Type | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `latitude`, `longitude` | `number` | Coordinates used by the provider (may be rounded). |
  | `timezone` | `string` | IANA timezone resolved for the coordinates. |
  | `timezone_abbreviation` | `string` | Abbreviation for the resolved timezone. |
  | `current` | `object` | Current observation: local `time`, `temperature_2m`, `weather_code`, and `wind_speed_10m`. |
  | `current_units` | `object` | Units for the current observation fields. |
  | `daily` | `object` | Daily arrays: `time`, `temperature_2m_max`, `temperature_2m_min`, `precipitation_probability_max`, `precipitation_sum`, and `weather_code`. |
  | `daily_units` | `object` | Units for the daily values. |
  
  ```json
  {
    "latitude": 35.69,
    "longitude": 51.39,
    "timezone": "Asia/Tehran",
    "timezone_abbreviation": "IRST",
    "current": {
      "time": "2026-11-17T12:00",
      "temperature_2m": 12.4,
      "weather_code": 3,
      "wind_speed_10m": 8.2
    },
    "current_units": {
      "temperature_2m": "°C",
      "weather_code": "wmo code",
      "wind_speed_10m": "km/h"
    },
    "daily": {
      "time": ["2026-11-17"],
      "temperature_2m_max": [15.1],
      "temperature_2m_min": [8.0],
      "precipitation_probability_max": [10],
      "precipitation_sum": [0.0],
      "weather_code": [3]
    },
    "daily_units": {
      "temperature_2m_max": "°C",
      "temperature_2m_min": "°C",
      "precipitation_probability_max": "%",
      "precipitation_sum": "mm",
      "weather_code": "wmo code"
    }
  }
  ```
  
  ## Errors
  
  - `400` — a coordinate is missing, not numeric, or outside its valid range; either date is missing/invalid, before today, more than 14 days ahead, or `end_date` is before `start_date`. The response contains an `error` message. For dates outside the allowed window, the message includes the latest supported date.
  - `401` — access token is missing or invalid.
  - `403` — requester is not the owner of the specified group.
  - `404` — the specified group does not exist.
  - `502` — Open-Meteo is unavailable, returns an unsuccessful response, or returns data that cannot be used.
}
